and many more things which help us with analytical

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:26.590
thinking.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:30.790
They have some really interesting puzzles
on their website which you can visit using

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.610
the link in the description below!

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.590
And hey, they ship their puzzles worldwide!

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:44.240
So here’s your first clue: you need to find
the COUNTRY Puzzle master is based in.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.609
Keep watching the video to know how this clue
can be used.

00:01:47.609 --> 00:01:53.469
First, let us understand a simple and logical
way to solve it.

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:58.829
As there are 3 things involved, we can use
3 variables for the heights.

00:01:58.829 --> 00:02:04.509
Let the heights of the stand, the standing
cat and the seated dog be ‘s’, ‘c’,

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:06.399
and ‘d’ respectively.

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:10.899
Now look at the first situation which is on
the left.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:16.750
Using simple math, we can say that the height
of the stand plus the height of the cat, minus

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:21.860
the height of the dog will be equal to one
hundred and fifty centimetres.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:27.860
Mathematically, we can write it as ‘s’
plus ‘c’ minus ‘d’ is equal to one

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.810
hundred and fifty!

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:36.530
Similarly, can you write an equation for the
second situation?

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:42.700
We can say that ‘s’ plus ‘d’ minus
‘c’ is equal to one hundred and twenty!

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:46.650
Can we find ‘s’ using just these two equations?

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.420
Of course we can!

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.500
We just have to ADD them!

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.680
‘c’ and ‘negative c’ cancel out.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:57.020
And ‘d’ and ‘negative d’ cancel out.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:00.940
What we have on the left hand side is ‘2
times s’.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:10.050
On the right hand side, we have the sum of
150 and 120 which is two hundred and seventy!

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:15.120
Dividing both sides by 2 will give us the
value of ‘s’ as one hundred and thirty

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.700
five centimeters!

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.600
That’s the height of the stand!

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.720
Well done to those who got the correct answer!

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.150
And this is your second clue.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:30.870
Keep watching to know how you can use the
first two clues!

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.980
There’s also a visual way to solve the riddle!

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:40.460
All we need to do is place one table on top
of the other like this ! Notice that this

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.180
length is ‘c’ units, and this length is
also ‘c’ units.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:49.760
It means we can get these lengths down by
‘c’ units.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.400
What if we move both these lengths down together
by ‘c’ units?

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.850
This is how it will look.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:58.970
What does this give us now?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:04.270
It tells us that the sum of the heights of
the tables is equal to the sum of these two

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:05.270
lengths!

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:09.450
So ‘2 times s’ will be equal to two hundred
and seventy centimetres.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:16.380
That gives us the value of ‘s’ as ‘one
hundred and thirty five centimetres’.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.720
The visual way was much faster right?

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.780
Absolutely!

